# 001 - every Value type (§3) through `print`, in its one display form:
# nil, the decimal digits, true/false, and a Str printed UNQUOTED.
# `-42` is unary minus applied to the literal 42: §6/.41 has no signed literals.
--- source
print nil;
print 0;
print -42;
print 9223372036854775807;
print true;
print false;
print "unquoted";
--- expect
nil
0
-42
9223372036854775807
true
false
unquoted
